Adding an interceptor to axios globally should add the interceptor every time axios is imported in other modules:

```js
import axios from 'axios';

axios.interceptors.request.use(
  (config) => {
    config.withCredentials = true;
    return config;
  },
  (error) =>
    Promise.reject(error),
);

// Another file
import axios from 'axios';
axios.get(...) // Includes interceptor
```

You can also add an interceptor to an axios instance:

```js
import axios from 'axios';

export API instance = axios.create()
API.interceptors.request.use(
  (config) => {
    config.withCredentials = true;
    return config;
  },
  (error) =>
    Promise.reject(error),
);

// Another file
import axios from 'axios';
import { API } from 'some/file.js'
API.get(...) // Includes interceptor
```

The second approach is preferred, so I'm not saying the change in this PR is an issue.
But as a quick fix I added a global interceptor to all axios calls, and `withCredentials` should have been added to every request.
(I had tested it and thought it worked)
If the global interceptor doesn't work, then we can remove it & need to refactor to use the `API` axios instance everywhere.

